<title>USA: WorldCorp Inc Q4 net falls after charge.</title>
<headline>WorldCorp Inc Q4 net falls after charge.</headline>
<dateline>HERNDON, Va 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary		$0.90		    $0.85</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 0.71		     0.69</p>
<p> Net			 13,877		   14,732</p>
<p> Revs			83,464		   57,963</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	15,386		   17,245</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	21,263		   23,155</p>
<p>		 Year</p>
<p> Shr primary loss$0.70	   profit $3.52</p>
<p> Shr diluted     n/a	     profit 2.82</p>
<p> Net	   loss11,754	  profit 60,208</p>
<p> Revs		313,672		  246,572</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary16,677		   17,104</p>
<p> Avg shrs dilutedn/a			22,995</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTES: The reduction in 1996 Q4 net earnings from the prior year's quarter resulted primarily from WorldCorp recording its 28.9 percent or $20.9 million of InteliData Technologies Corp's one-time, noncash merger related charges of about $72.3 million.</p>
<p>The reduction was partially offset by an increase in net gains from issuances and purchases of equity by the company's subsidiaries, from $18.7 million in Q4 1995 to $37.2 million in Q4 1996.</p>
